This is already in the structured JSON format output. There is no need to convert the input into the structured JSON format. However, if you want to add a new function to the output list, you can do so like this:

```json
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "<function_name_1>",
            "code": "<code_of_function_1>",
            "vulnerability": "<short_vulnera_desc_1>",
            "reason": "<reason_1>"
        },
        {
            "function_name": "<function_name_2>",
            "code": "<code_of_function_2>",
            "vulnerability": "<short_vulnera_desc_2>",
            "reason": "<reason_2>"
        },
        {
            "function_name": "<function_name_3>",
            "code": "<code_of_function_3>",
            "vulnerability": "<short_vulnera_desc_3>",
            "reason": "<reason_3>"
        }
    ]
}
```
Just replace `<function_name>`, `<code_of_function>`, `<short_vulnera_desc>` and `<reason>` with the respective information for the new function.